From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0180: backboardd is not a platform binary

dyld discards DYLD_* for a platform binary. This port marks every root-filesystem
binary as one in its AMFI stand-in, which is why the injected environment never
reached the window server. Cleared for that executable alone.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5797,6 +5797,15 @@
 		 * startup (seventeen execs, not one crash). Clear it for this one binary.
 		 */
 		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_REQUIRE_LV;
+		/*
+		 * hakios (the reference port) lets dyld honour DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES by not
+		 * marking root-filesystem binaries as platform binaries at all; this port
+		 * does mark them (0035), and dyld throws every DYLD_* variable away for a
+		 * platform binary. Clear the flag for the window server only, so the
+		 * environment injected by 0175 reaches it.
+		 */
+		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
+		printf("sweet: backboardd is not a platform binary; dyld reads its environment\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd may load a library that is not Apple's\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is marked debuggable so dyld takes its DYLD_* variables\n");
 		static const char *const extra[] = {
